147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Guest Investigator \(GI\) Program: A substantial portion of Swift's observing time is allocated to the GI program. Scientists from around the world can submit proposals to use Swift's instruments \(BAT, XRT, and UVOT\) to observe a wide variety of astrophysical phenomena. Blazars are frequently proposed targets due to their highly variable nature and broad-band emission. These proposals are peer-reviewed, and successful ones are scheduled during the periods when Swift isn't actively responding to a GRB.)
/E (Guest Investigator \(GI\) Program: A substantial portion of Swift's observing time is allocated to the GI program. Scientists from around the world can submit proposals to use Swift's instruments \(BAT, XRT, and UVOT\) to observe a wide variety of astrophysical phenomena. Blazars are frequently proposed targets due to their highly variable nature and broad-band emission. These proposals are peer-reviewed, and successful ones are scheduled during the periods when Swift isn't actively responding to a GRB.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Target of Opportunity \(ToO\) Program: Blazars are known for their extreme and rapid variability across the electromagnetic spectrum, often undergoing dramatic flares. When a blazar undergoes a significant outburst \(e.g., in gamma-rays detected by Fermi-LAT, or at other wavelengths\), scientists can submit a ToO request to Swift. This triggers rapid observations of the flaring blazar, allowing Swift's XRT and UVOT to capture the evolving spectral and temporal characteristics of the flare.)
/E (Target of Opportunity \(ToO\) Program: Blazars are known for their extreme and rapid variability across the electromagnetic spectrum, often undergoing dramatic flares. When a blazar undergoes a significant outburst \(e.g., in gamma-rays detected by Fermi-LAT, or at other wavelengths\), scientists can submit a ToO request to Swift. This triggers rapid observations of the flaring blazar, allowing Swift's XRT and UVOT to capture the evolving spectral and temporal characteristics of the flare.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
