/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Level 0: These are the raw telemetry files directly downlinked from the spacecraft. They represent the fundamental, unprocessed data stream from the instruments. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Level 1: At this stage, raw telemetry is converted into FITS files, undergoing minimal initial processing. For instance, UVOT raw images are provided at this level \(sw[obsid]u[filter]_rw.img.gz\). These files serve as the initial structured data for subsequent instrument-specific processing. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Level 2: This level comprises calibrated event lists and cleaned sky images, produced after rigorous data screening and coordinate transformations. Most users typically commence their scientific analysis with these files. Examples include cleaned XRT event files \(sw[obsid]xpc_cl.evt.gz\) and UVOT sky coordinate images \(sw[obsid]u[filter]_sk.img.gz\). These data are corrected for instrumental effects and mapped to celestial coordinates, making them ready for scientific interpretation. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Level 3: These are higher-level science products, automatically generated from the Level 2 files. This includes products such as light curves \(sw[obsid]xpc_lc.fits\) and spectra \(sw[obsid]xpc_spec.fits\). These products are directly usable for scientific interpretation and publication. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
